From bce1144cd47771e6c894b9c5d18739f1669cf984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 08:20:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add severity classification to AI inspection findings

Every new_finding is now classified major (structural/safety damage:
dents, cracks, broken lights/mirrors, torn seats), minor (cosmetic:
scratches, paint chips, stone chips) or dirty (cleanliness: mud,
stains, dirty carpets/boot). The analyze-inspection edge function's
prompt now works through an exhaustive per-category defect checklist
covering exterior, windscreen, interior and boot instead of relying
on the model to notice issues unprompted, and severity feeds into
the condition score (major damage weighs far more than a dirty seat)
and the owner-facing summary/recommendation text.

The mobile app colour-codes findings by severity end to end: red for
major, orange for minor, yellow for dirty, matching the same key on
both the per-shot bounding-box overlay and the top-level new-findings
list on the owner's Vehicle Health Report.
